      "side": 1,
      "message": "`operations` shouldn\u0027t be null here, since we create it on line 426.\n\nFWIW, I know this function looks a bit odd. It matches the behavior of the framework `constructInsertOperations` function, which will create a new list of operations if one doesn\u0027t exist, else will edit in place the list you provide. This lets us easily drop the old batch and put a new one on top below by passing null to the function.\n\nI wrote this code to match the `constructInsertOperationsForContacts` function above, and its usage too (which also, FWIW, I know looks sparse, but it gets used way more with my caching change!). And _that_ code was just taken from how it _used_ to work in the old objects. I didn\u0027t really want to mess with years old code for contacts storage yet (though that\u0027s on the mental backlog).",
